TITLE:»
TAKE A STEP AND BECOME A WONDER.

BIBLE REFERENCE:» 
DEUTERONOMY 2:3 (KJV) "Ye have compassed this mountain long enough: turn you northward." 

It is no doubt that a journey of one thousand miles must begin with a step of faith.  To step into your wonderland, you must step out of your comfort zone.  So, it was with the children of Israel when God instructed them to leave Egypt for the promised land.  At one point while that journey lasted, they chose to remain in a particular mountain because of the numerous challenges on their way.  For them, that was safer since defeating the dwellers of Canaan was no small deal.  But, understand that what lunches men into a world of wonders is the giant stride they make towards actualizing their dreams.  This is without prejudice to the risks, stress, pains and sometimes, mockery you may encounter while heading for your aspiration (Hebrews 12:2 "Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before Him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is (today) set down at the right hand of the throne of God).  Therefore, for you to take steps into the destiny that God has for you, you must despise your fears and shame.  

The truth is, no matter how long you abide, without stepping out you are not likely to arrive your destination.  This is why it is important to take that step NOW in the direction God is prompting you.  It might be in the direction of getting a life partner, starting up a business idea, inventing a product or going into ministry work at a time your finance is in shambles.  I will say, trust God and dare to take a step!  What do I mean by this?  For example, someone that is expecting a child from God should step out by faith and start buying baby items!  

The Bible recorded series of Scriptures that assured that God Himself will direct the steps you make ( 1 Thessalonians 3:11; Proverbs 3:6; Psalm 1:6 and Proverbs 11:5).  And if God leads, you are sure to arrive at your expectation.  Before now, I worry about making decision.  I used to be afraid to step out in faith.  I would think, what if I fail?  I was so scared of failing, I would muddle around in indecision for weeks.  Then one day I found out it was not my power that was going to carry it out anyway.

There is something supernatural with taking step of faith.  When you dare step-out in faith, God steps-in to lead the way and thereby making you a wonder to behold.  The Psamist would say "I am as a  wonder unto many" (Ps. 71:7).  More often than none, God waits for you to take a step then He will walk the remaining miles for you.  I have heard people say, "am waiting on God" but the actual truth remains that God has always waited for us to act in faith.  The Almighty God is not sluggish for anyone to say I am waiting on God (2 Peter 3:9 "The Lord is not slack concerning his promise").  Some Christians have taken time of prayer and fasting as time of waiting for God to show up in their cases.  Whereas it is suppose to be a time of empowering our faith at the altar of prayer to take delivery of what God has already provided.  

For River Jordan to part for Israelites to pass through, God told Joshua to instruct the Priests to go out and make the sole of their feet to touch the waters (Joshua 3:15-16).  Sometimes you will have to reach out for that goal first before God will be attracted to fulfilling it.  God establishes our goings and not our waiting (Psalm 40:2 "...and set my feet upon a rock, and established my goings").  Also, Psalm 23:6 supported this by saying "...goodness and mercy shall follow you".  This means that the goodness and mercy is for the person who has stepped out in faith and not the one that is waiting.  Therefore, it is our step of faith that God backs up.  No step, no backup!

As this year comes to an end, I can tell you free of charge that God can still do everything in your 2018 expectation list, but you must decide to take a step first.  He has provided the power.  He has provided His Name.  He has provided the Blood of Jesus.  He has even made us partakers of His kingdom (Colossians 1:12).  So, take that step today and become a wonder to your world!

In conclusion, is God leading you in some new direction?  Is He leading you to step out in faith for healing, marriage or prosperity or to take a whole new step of ministry?  Do not let fear hold you back anymore!

FURTHER READING:» 
Romans 4:13-21.  

But, most importantly, you must receive Jesus Christ as Saviour to be able to make the right step that will lunch you into wonders in life. Therefore, if you are here but you have never asked Jesus to come into your heart and become your Personal Lord and Saviour or you did sometime ago but you have gone back?  What I mean to say is, ARE YOU BORN AGAIN?  If your answer is "NO", or you are not sure.  Please, I want to pray with you.  Pray this prayer with all sincerity and confidence:

PRAYER: 
Lord Jesus, I come to you today! I am a sinner, I can't help myself. Forgive me my sins. Cleanse me with your precious blood. Deliver me from sin and Satan, to serve the Living God. Today, Lord Jesus, I accept you as my Lord and Saviour. Thank you Jesus for saving me! Now I declare, I am born again! Amen.

REMAIN EVER BLESSED!!

JESUS IS LORD!!!

