 TITLE:»
ENGAGING THE POWER IN THE NAME - JESUS.

 BIBLE REFERENCE:»
JOHN 14:13 (The Amplified Bible) "And I will do [I Myself will grant] whatever you may ask in My name [as presenting all that I AM,] so that the Father may be glorified and extolled in (through) the Son."

Child of God!  Did you know that there is more to the  Name of Jesus Christ than a mere phrase we add to the end of our prayers.  Let us understand that all God is and does is represented in the Name of Jesus.  The Amplified Bible says when you ask in His Name, you present your requests to the Father on the basis of all that Jesus is.  You also glorify God when you pray in that Name.  So you can boldly expect to have those requests granted and not because you are worthy, but because the Lord Jesus is.

The Name of Jesus carries authority over all other names.  In Philippians 2:5-11, the Apostle Paul tells us, "God also hath highly exalted him [Jesus], and given him a name which is above every name: that at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth."

In spite of all the Word of God has to say about the power of the Name of Jesus, most believers do not seem to put much interest in it.  They will pray in the Name of Jesus, then turn right around and say, "I hope God has answered that prayer."  This is so, because they do not realize that if they only had the faith to believe it, Jesus' Name alone carries enough authority to guarantee the answers to their prayers (James 1:6-8 "But let him ask in  faith, nothing wavering. For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with  the wind and tossed. For let not that man think that he shall receive any thing of  the Lord. A double minded man  is unstable in all his ways").

They even let religious slang rob them of the power of using that Name.  I have heard many well-meaning believers end their prayers with the phrase, "For Jesus' sake."  But Jesus did not say we should pray for His sake.  He said you should pray in His Name.  That's all!  When you have obeyed that little biblical instruction, then you are on your way to receiving your request no matter what they are. 

Therefore, learn to dig in to the Word of God yourself and find out just how much power and authority the Name of Jesus holds for your cases.  Use that power every time you pray.  Stop hoping God will answer you but rather start expecting Him to cause every circumstance in your life to bow its knee in honour of that glorious Name of Jesus.  I SEE YOU ARRIVING YOUR GLORIOUS DESTINY IN THIS NEW WEEK IN JESUS' MIGHTY NAME! AMEN.

